<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Gjergj Arianiti</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1383–<a href="/years/1462">1462</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Gjergj Arianiti was an Albanian lord of the Arianiti family, whose lands lay in central Albania along the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shkumbin">Shkumbin</a> valley. Once a hostage at the Ottoman court, he led a revolt against the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottomans</a> from 1432 and won several victories. He later allied with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/skanderbeg">Skanderbeg</a>, who married his daughter Andronika, in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/league-of-lezhe">League of Lezhë</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/gjergj-arianiti.jpg" alt="Gjergj Arianiti" width="320" height="478" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Thomas Quine · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:GjergjArianitiBust.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
